bg3le preload: stand up bg3se's globals (gStaticSymbols, gExtender) in bg3le's own setup, not only from the overlay

On top of 0001-0012. extender_globals_init() (src/vendor/extender_globals.cpp) is what creates
bg3se::gStaticSymbols and bg3se::gExtender, and its only caller was imgui_overlay_start(), which builds once the
engine heap exists: in practice from bg3le's vkCreateInstance export (src/vulkan_forward.cpp). Entity reads need
gStaticSymbols too: a component that is still pending goes through EntityWorld::Deferred, which indexes its
command buffers by ThreadRegistry::RequestThreadIndex(), read through gStaticSymbols. In a game where the
overlay never built (BG3LE_IMGUI=0, or Vulkan calls that never reach bg3le's exports), the first such read
crashed: SIGSEGV at 0xa0, pc ThreadRegistry::RequestThreadIndex+0xa, rax 0, from bg3le_entity_pending_component
at the first server tick after Running (issue #101; reproduced with BG3LE_IMGUI=0 on the pinned build).

- ensure_symbols() (the first Osiris callback, RegisterDIVFunctions, about 1 s before vkCreateInstance) calls
  extender_globals_init() last, after install_game_allocator(): the globals allocate from the engine heap, and
  that is the first point it is installed, which is why the overlay waited for it. Earlier, next to the "bg3le,
  bg3se vNN API" line, the heap isn't there yet. Without the heap it logs "extender: globals not stood up: no
  engine heap"; an exception is logged, not passed into the Osiris callback.
- extender_globals_init() is idempotent (a mutex and g_ready), so the overlay's own call later finds them and
  builds on the same objects. What it reads that early is safe: the targets it resolves (PathRoots,
  TextureAtlasMap, the thread-index read) are found by scanning the image, which needs no symbol table, and
  PathRoots entries the engine has not filled yet read as unset.
- With the overlay off, the extra objects change nothing else: the SDL hooks pass events on while enableUI_ is
  false, the overlay tick returns until the overlay started, and OnCreateWindow binds only an initialized UI.
  Path overrides now resolve to absolute paths as they do in an overlay launch.

Offline: tools/test_bg3le_patches.py checks the call in the patched source. The fix itself needs the game: a
launch with BG3LE_IMGUI=0 must log "extender: globals stood up" and read entities at Running without the crash,
and a normal launch must be unchanged. Against bg3le 3728a68 (v0.3.6) with 0001-0012. Applied by
tools/build_bg3le.sh.
---
diff --git a/src/preload.cpp b/src/preload.cpp
index 05c0f80..0fb9f87 100644
--- a/src/preload.cpp
+++ b/src/preload.cpp
@@ -22,6 +22,7 @@
 #include <chrono>
 #include <thread>
 #include <mutex>
+#include <exception>
 #include <ctime>
 #include <unistd.h>
 
@@ -54,6 +55,8 @@ namespace bg3le {
 // Defined in src/vendor/imgui_overlay.cpp, which needs bg3se headers this
 // file does not include.
 void imgui_overlay_start();
+// Defined in src/vendor/extender_globals.cpp, for the same reason.
+void extender_globals_init();
 
 
 namespace {
@@ -79,6 +82,7 @@ extern "C" bool bg3le_stats_attr_at(void const* object, std::size_t index,
 extern "C" bool bg3le_stats_attr_set(void const* object, std::size_t index,
                                      int raw);
 extern "C" bool bg3le_install_game_allocator(void* alloc, void* free);
+extern "C" bool bg3le_game_allocator_ready();
 extern "C" void bg3le_corelib_strings_install();
 
 // Points bg3se's GameAllocRaw/GameFree at the engine's own heap, so any bg3se
@@ -513,6 +517,27 @@ void ensure_symbols() {
         install_game_allocator();
         fast_alloc_install();
         install_path_override_hook();
+        // bg3se's globals (gStaticSymbols, gExtender) are not the overlay's
+        // alone: an entity read whose component is still pending goes through
+        // EntityWorld::Deferred, which takes its command buffer by
+        // ThreadRegistry::RequestThreadIndex() through gStaticSymbols. The
+        // overlay was their only creator, from bg3le's vkCreateInstance
+        // export, so a game where that never ran (BG3LE_IMGUI=0, or Vulkan
+        // calls that bypass the preload) crashed at the first such read
+        // (SIGSEGV at 0xa0). Stood up here, the first point the engine heap
+        // they allocate from is installed (above); the overlay's own call,
+        // later, then finds them.
+        if (!bg3le_game_allocator_ready()) {
+            logf("extender: globals not stood up: no engine heap");
+        } else {
+            try {
+                extender_globals_init();
+            } catch (std::exception const& e) {
+                logf("extender: could not stand up the globals: %s", e.what());
+            } catch (...) {
+                logf("extender: could not stand up the globals");
+            }
+        }
     });
 }
 
